Let $f(x)$ be the function defined for all non-zero real numbers $x$ by $$f(x) = \left\{
\begin{array}{cl}
x^3 - 3x^2 + 4 & \text{if } x < 1, \\
ax^3 + bx^2 + c & \text{if } x \ge 1.
\end{array}
\right.$$If $f(f(x)) = f(x)$ infinitely many times, over all non-zero real numbers $x,$ determine the constants $a,$ $b,$ and $c$ in the form $x = 1 + \frac ab$ where $a$ and $b$ are integers and determine $|a + b |$.

